{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And men of the children of Israel.</b> And who are they? Elitzur son of Shedeur and his companions. And even though Scripture did not name them explicitly, it gave identifying signs. It is written here: ״ואנשים מבני ישראל״, and it is written there: ״האנשים האלה אשר נקבו בשמות״. It is written here: ״נשיאי עדה קריאי מועד״, and it is written there: ״אלה קריאי העדה נשיאי מטות״. A parable: a prominent young man who was found stealing vessels in the bathhouse. The owner of the stolen goods did not want to publicize him, so he began giving identifying signs. They said to him: Who stole your vessels? He says to them: a prominent young man who is tall, whose eyes are fine, whose hair is black and whose locks are curly, and whose nose is upturned. Once he gave these signs, they recognized him. So too here — even though Scripture left them unspecified, through the signs you know who they are. Come and see how severe dispute is: a heavenly court does not punish until one is twenty, and below [thirteen]; but here even nursing infants were punished, as it is written: ״הם ובניהם וטפם״. And likewise they said: Great is peace, for even the Holy One, blessed be He, altered in it [i.e., deviated from the truth for its sake], as we explained above."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:34.519027957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}